  "step_3": "The decision reason requires a focus on the maximum loss (i.e., the worst outcome) and a weighting of losses as more important than gains. While Lottery B does have a better minimum outcome (3000 vs. 0), the individual does not reference the worst-case scenario or frame 0 Euros as a 'loss' in a psychological or decisional sense. Instead, the justification is based on the certainty of winning, which aligns more with risk aversion or a certainty effect rather than a loss-focused reasoning. There is no indication that the individual treated the 0 Euro outcome as a salient loss or applied a loss-gain asymmetry. Therefore, although the choice aligns with what the reason would recommend, the underlying rationale expressed in the verbal report does not match the structure or emphasis of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
